From: Joseph <162703152+josephnef@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 22:04:10 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] kestrel: park the EDCCA level on 5 GHz as on 6 GHz (#491)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

## The problem

Host injection from an 8832CU goes silent on the upper 5 GHz channels.
With the BB table's EDCCA level the MAC energy-detect TX gate latches
busy on the receiver's own floor (-65..-69 dBm as the BB measures it, no
DIG), the mechanism the 6 GHz path already parks
(`src/kestrel/CLAUDE.md`). Measured on the bench (TX50UH injector, 20 ms
gap, 8812CU witness, default configuration):

| channel | witnessed of ~435 |
|---|---|
| 6 / 36 / 44 | 205 / 192 / 211 |
| 52 / 60 / 64 | 226 / 92 / 12 |
| 100 / 149 / 157 / 161 | 0 |

SDR airtime on ch161 under a max-duty flood: 0.0% (ch44: +4% over idle);
the injector stalls on bulk-OUT timeouts. The fixed TX-power knob (8 /
14 / 20 dBm) changes nothing. `DEVOURER_CCA_GATES=0,1` (EDCCA gate alone
cleared) restores ch64 / 100 / 161 to 220-226; `1,0` (primary alone)
restores nothing. The tune log says it on every 5 GHz tune: `EDCCA band1
pwdB fb=-67 ... busy=1`.

## The change

`kestrel_halbb_edcca_6g` becomes `kestrel_halbb_edcca_park(band_type,
bw)` and the channel set calls it for 5 GHz as well as 6 GHz: the
vendor's unlinked `EDCCA_NORMAL_MODE` level, its own level for an
unassociated device, never busy. Preamble carrier sense stays on. 2.4
GHz is untouched (floor -82 dBm, busy=0). Comments and the Kestrel notes
carry the measurements; the compliance consequence the 6 GHz note
already states now covers 5 GHz.

## Measured after the change

Default configuration, same setup: ch6 196/423, ch44 215/434, ch100
227/440, ch161 224/437. Deferral still holds on ch161: a max-duty 6M
injector sent 19063 frames in 8 s on a quiet channel, 7327 (7086
witnessed) under a co-channel max-duty MCS1 flood with the gates on,
15676 (10639) with `DEVOURER_DIS_CCA=1`. Linux build + `ctest` 83/83.

One bench, one injecting unit (the second TX50UH on this bench does not
host-inject at all, on any band, for an unrelated reason tracked in
#490), near field.

Part of #490.

